Key Points
return exits the current function call - it doesn't call anything new

Control returns to where that function was called from

The next line after the recursive call is always the backtracking step (board[row][j] = '.')

This pattern continues until all possibilities are tried

This is how recursive backtracking explores all solutions - by carefully unwinding the call stack and trying alternative paths at each decision point.

